        "proseEntries": 22,
        "figureReferenceText": "这里讨论的变压器由闭合铁芯和套在铁芯上的两个导线线圈组成，有些变压器具有两个以上的线圈，如图 $58$ 所示。\n连接交流电源的线圈叫做**初级绕组**，向用电仪器或设备这一“负载”供电的线圈叫做**次级绕组**。\n\n图 $59$ 表示双绕组变压器的结构，图 $60$ 给出它的简化电路符号。\n初级和次级的名称由电源侧与负载侧的连接关系决定，并不直接表示哪侧电压更高。",
        "readCompletely": true,
        "figureCompatibilityOnly": true,
        "wholeTextRecheckOrApproval": false
      },
      {
        "edition": "modern-us-neutral-en",
        "file": {
          "path": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/stemrobin-181-six/lemmadeck/.tmp/STEMROBIN-181/d1816-d739/work/adapt/10p/modern-us-neutral-en/lessons/phy10-c1-s4-n33/lesson.template.json",
          "bytes": 35180,
          "sha256": "3816ede7f440591976802d874ce947a50595ecd33deb29461d0c0593cf3cac44"
        },
        "proseEntries": 22,
        "figureReferenceText": "The transformer considered here has a closed iron core and two wire coils around it, although some transformers have more than two coils, as indicated in Figure $58$.\nThe coil connected to the alternating source is the **primary winding**, and the coil supplying the instruments or equipment called the \"load\" is the **secondary winding**.\n\nFigure $59$ shows the two-winding structure, and Figure $60$ gives its simplified circuit symbol.\nThe names primary and secondary identify the source side and load side, not necessarily the higher-voltage and lower-voltage sides.",
        "readCompletely": true,
        "figureCompatibilityOnly": true,
        "wholeTextRecheckOrApproval": false
      }
